  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A car of mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> is navigating a banked circular road of radius <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"r\"></span> at a constant speed <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v\"></span>. There is no friction between the tires and the road. What is the correct expression for the angle <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\theta\"></span> of banking that allows the car to stay on the road without slipping?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\tan\\theta = \\dfrac{v^2}{gr}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\tan\\theta = \\dfrac{gr}{v^2}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\tan\\theta = \\dfrac{v}{gr}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\tan\\theta = \\dfrac{v^2r}{g}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
  },
